{
    "background_story": "Giselle was a rising star in the 1920s New York City jazz scene. As a saxophonist, she was known for her smooth sounds and stylish stage presence. Her signature look was a tailored, pinstriped suit, complete with a fedora and a sparkly brooch. Giselle's music was a fusion of traditional jazz and modern swing, captivating audiences at iconic venues like the Cotton Club. Her pinstriped attire became a symbol of her unique sound and flair, earning her the nickname 'The Pinstriped Siren.' As her fame grew, so did her influence, inspiring a new generation of female musicians to take the stage. Giselle's legacy continued to swing through the decades, her pinstriped suit remaining an iconic representation of her trailblazing spirit.",
